<!-- ============ 4. Synaptix CoS density visualizer ============ -->
<section class="sec sec--dark" id="cos" aria-labelledby="cos-title">
  <div class="wrap cos">
    <div class="cos__copy rv">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark"><span>Synaptix<sup class="tm">&#8482;</sup> CoS · Capacity of Servers You Own</span></p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="cos-title">Less overhead per workload. More room on hardware you already paid for.</h2>
      <p>Traditional virtual machines each carry their own overhead. Synaptix<sup class="tm">&#8482;</sup> CoS uses a lighter way to run workloads, so less of every host goes to virtualization and more goes to the work. It has been demonstrated in lab and data center environments, and validation for wider deployment is still under way.</p>
      <p class="cos__fine">[CONFIRM: product name "Synaptix<sup class="tm">&#8482;</sup> CoS" (the site currently says "Synaptik<sup class="tm">&#8482;</sup> Cell") and its availability status]</p>
      <a class="btn btn--grad btn--mag" href="#contact" data-topic="Something else"><span>Ask about CoS</span><svg class="ic"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
    </div>
    <div class="dens" data-dens>
      <div class="dens__top">
        <div class="seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Execution model">
          <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="true" data-mode="vm">Traditional VMs</button>
          <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-mode="cos">Synaptix<sup class="tm">&#8482;</sup> CoS</button>
